-- title:
--   Chart-level package at a supersingular point over the X₀(Mp) node
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, subject to the tameness conditions that either $p\ne 2$ or some prime $\ell\mid M$ has $\ell\not\equiv 1\pmod 4$, and that if $p=3$ some prime $\ell\mid M$ has $\ell\not\equiv 1\pmod 3$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a $p$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$, $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K_1\supseteq K_2$ be the intermediate fields of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as the $L$-subfields generated by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion fields $\mathtt{x1x0FunctionFieldC}\ \mathbb Q\ M\ p$ (level $\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p)$) and $\mathtt{qExpFunctionFieldC}\ \mathbb Q\ \Gamma_0(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ containing $\zeta$ in its image and with $p$ in its maximal ideal, uniformiser $\varpi$, acting compatibly on $K_1$ and $K_2$; let $j\in K_1$, $j_2\in K_2$ be nonzero elements whose Laurent expansions are both $\mathtt{coeffEmb}\ L\ \mathtt{jq}$. Write $A_i$ for the chart ring $\mathtt{chartAlgFin}$, i.e. the elements of $K_i$ integral over $A[j]$ resp. $A[j_2]$, and $\mathcal X_i=\mathtt{TwoChartIntegralModel}$ for the corresponding pushout of the two chart spectra over $A$. Assume given a morphism $\pi_2:\mathcal X_1\to\mathcal X_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec}A$ and an $A$-algebra map $\iota:A_2\to A_1$ compatible with the Laurent embeddings, such that $\iota$ and $\pi_2$ match on the $j$-finite charts, $\pi_2$ pulls the finite chart of $\mathcal X_2$ back to that of $\mathcal X_1$, both $\pi_2$ and $\iota$ are finite, and $A_1$ consists exactly of the elements of $K_1$ integral over the image of $\iota$. Let $z\in\mathcal X_1$ be a point at which the germ of $\varpi$ (pulled back along the structure morphism) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, let $y\in\operatorname{Spec}A_1$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y)=z$, and assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:A_1\to\Omega$ with kernel $\mathfrak y:=y$ the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathtt{ssJSet}\ p\ \Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $p$-torsion point. Then, with $A_1$ an $A_2$-algebra via $\iota$: $A_2$ and $A_1$ are Noetherian, $\iota$ is injective, $\mathfrak y$ is maximal with finite residue ring $A_1/\mathfrak y$, and $A_1$ has fraction field $K_1$; moreover, assuming $\mathfrak y$ prime, the adic completion of $(A_1)_{\mathfrak y}$ at its maximal ideal is an integrally closed domain, every non-maximal prime of $(A_1)_{\mathfrak y}$ is unramified over $A_2$, and for every $w\in\mathbb N$, every complete discrete valuation domain $W_2$ with a ring homomorphism $\sigma_2:A\to W_2$ sending $\varpi$ to a uniformiser, and every ring isomorphism $e_2$ from the adic completion of the stalk of $\mathcal X_2$ at $\pi_2(z)$ onto $\mathtt{UVCrossingModel}\ W_2\ ((\sigma_2\varpi)^{(p-1)w})$ carrying germs of elements $a\in A$ to the constants $\sigma_2 a$, one has that $w$ is a unit in $W_2$ whenever $p\nmid w$, and, assuming $\iota^{-1}\mathfrak y$ prime, there is a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $(A_2)_{\iota^{-1}\mathfrak y}$ onto the same $\mathtt{UVCrossingModel}\ W_2\ ((\sigma_2\varpi)^{(p-1)w})$ again carrying the image of each $a\in A$ to the constant $\sigma_2 a$.
--
--   This is the chart-level package at a supersingular point of the integral model of the curve of level $\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p)$ over the corresponding node of $X_0(Mp)$: it collects in one conjunction the Noetherianity, finiteness, fraction-field, analytic normality, pointed unramifiedness and node-transfer inputs needed there. It is cited by [`ModularCurve.XOneGammaZeroP.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_of_tame`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneGammaZeroP.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_of_tame), which produces the crossing-model description of the completed local ring at such a point.
